(1430,3005,'Infection of the nose, sinuses, trachea (windpipe), bronchi, bronchioles or lungs.','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:09',NULL,NULL,'3513FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1431,3006,'A major affective disorder marked by severe mood swings (manic or major depressive episodes) and a tendency to remission and recurrence.','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:09',NULL,NULL,'3509FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1432,3007,'A major affective disorder marked by severe mood swings (manic or major depressive episodes) and a tendency to remission and recurrence.','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:09',NULL,NULL,'3507FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1433,3009,'A skin condition characterized by the development of recurring boils.','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:09',NULL,NULL,'112FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1434,3010,'A pathological condition that can suddenly affect the hemodynamic equilibrium, usually manifested by failure to perfuse or oxygenate vital organs.','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:09',NULL,NULL,'3499FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1435,3011,'Difficult childbirth or labor.','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:09',NULL,NULL,'3497FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1436,3012,'A transient loss of consciousness and postural tone caused by diminished blood flow to the brain (i.e., BRAIN ISCHEMIA). Presyncope refers to the sensation of lightheadedness and loss of strength that precedes a syncopal event or accompanies an incomplete syncope. (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, pp367-9)','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:09',NULL,NULL,'3485FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1437,3013,'Conditions characterized by disturbances of usual sleep patterns or behaviors. Sleep disorders may be divided into three major categories: DYSSOMNIAS (i.e. disorders characterized by insomnia or hypersomnia), PARASOMNIAS (abnormal sleep behaviors), and sleep disorders secondary to medical or psychiatric disorders. (From Thorpy, Sleep Disorders Medicine, 1994, p187)','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:09',NULL,NULL,'3474FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1438,3015,'An unpleasant sensation induced by noxious stimuli and generally received by specialized nerve endings.','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:09',NULL,NULL,'15592FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1439,3019,'A cognitive disorder characterized by an impaired ability to comprehend written and printed words or phrases despite intact vision. This condition may be developmental or acquired. Developmental dyslexia is marked by reading achievement that falls substantially below that expected given the individual&#39;s chronological age, measured intelligence, and age-appropriate education. The disturbance in reading significantly interferes with academic achievement or with activities of daily living that require reading skills. (From DSM-IV)','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:09',NULL,NULL,'3450FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1440,3022,'A type of acneiform disorder in which secondary pyogenic infection in and around pilosebaceous structures ends in keloidal scarring. It manifests as persistent folliculitis of the back of the neck associated with occlusion of the follicular orifices. It is most often encountered in black or Asian men.','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:09',NULL,NULL,'15583FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1441,3023,'A chronic disorder of the pilosebaceous apparatus associated with an increase in sebum secretion. It is characterized by open comedones (blackheads), closed comedones (whiteheads), and pustular nodules. The cause is unknown, but heredity and age are predisposing factors.','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:09',NULL,NULL,'15578FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1442,3025,'Harm or hurt to the ankle or ankle joint usually inflicted by an external source.','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:09',NULL,NULL,'3430FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1443,3028,'A collective term for muscle and ligament injuries without dislocation or fracture. A sprain is a joint injury in which some of the fibers of a supporting ligament are ruptured but the continuity of the ligament remains intact. A strain is an overstretching or overexertion of some part of the musculature.','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:09',NULL,NULL,'3426FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1444,3030,'A disease of infants due to group 2 phage type 17 staphylococci that produce an epidermolytic exotoxin. Superficial fine vesicles and bullae form and rupture easily, resulting in loss of large sheets of epidermis.','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:09',NULL,NULL,'3417FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1445,3032,'Skin diseases characterized by local or general distributions of blisters. They are classified according to the site and mode of blister formation. Lesions can appear spontaneously or be precipitated by infection, trauma, or sunlight. Etiologies include immunologic and genetic factors. (From Scientific American Medicine, 1990)','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:09',NULL,NULL,'3378FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1446,3034,'Disorders related to substance abuse, the side effects of a medication, toxin exposure, and alcohol related disorders','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:10',NULL,NULL,'3374FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1447,3036,'General or unspecified injuries involving the fingers.','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:10',NULL,NULL,'15538FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1448,3039,'Clinical syndrome characterized by abdominal pain of great severity associated with other symptoms and signs, usually those of acute peritonitis, which might well be the result of a ruptured abdominal viscus or a similar abdominal catastrophe requiring urgent surgical operation.','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:10',NULL,NULL,'15521FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1449,3042,'A chronic, relapsing, inflammatory, and often febrile multisystemic disorder of connective tissue, characterized principally by involvement of the skin, joints, kidneys, and serosal membranes. It is of unknown etiology, but is thought to represent a failure of the regulatory mechanisms of the autoimmune system. The disease is marked by a wide range of system dysfunctions, an elevated erythrocyte sedimentation rate, and the formation of LE cells in the blood or bone marrow.','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:10',NULL,NULL,'3347FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1450,3046,'Acute inflammation of the vermiform appendix.','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:10',NULL,NULL,'15511FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1451,3047,'A variety of conditions affecting the anatomic and functional characteristics of the temporomandibular joint. Factors contributing to the complexity of temporomandibular diseases are its relation to dentition and mastication and the symptomatic effects in other areas which account for referred pain to the joint and the difficulties in applying traditional diagnostic procedures to temporomandibular joint pathology where tissue is rarely obtained and x-rays are often inadequate or nonspecific. Common diseases are developmental abnormalities, trauma, subluxation, luxation, arthritis, and neoplasia. (From Thoma&#39;s Oral Pathology, 6th ed, pp577-600)','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:10',NULL,NULL,'3339FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1452,3048,'Inflammation of the bronchioles. Including acute bronchiolitis due to respiratory syncitial virus, human metapneumovirus, other specified organisms or unspecified.','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:10',NULL,NULL,'15502FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1453,3049,'Downward displacement of the uterus. It is classified in various degrees: in the first degree the cervix is within the vaginal orifice; in the second degree the cervix is outside the orifice; in the third degree the entire uterus is outside the orifice.','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:10',NULL,NULL,'3331FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
