(1455,3051,'Condition of vaginal bleeding with or without pain in early pregnancy which may presage an abortion.','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:10',NULL,NULL,'3329FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1456,3052,'Disorders in which the symptoms are distressing to the individual and recognized by him or her as being unacceptable. Social relationships may be greatly affected but usually remain within acceptable limits. The disturbance is relatively enduring or recurrent without treatment.','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:10',NULL,NULL,'3328FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1457,3053,'A decrease in the number of blood platelets.','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:10',NULL,NULL,'3326FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1458,3054,'Inflammation of the thyroid gland.','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:10',NULL,NULL,'3317FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1459,3055,'DEF: Frequent and loose bowel movements of acute onset (&amp;lt; 24 hours).  DESC: Commonly associated with abdominal pain. May be associated with blood or mucus in the stool. REF: http://www.healthatoz.com/healthatoz/Atoz/common/standard/transform.jsp?requestURI=/healthatoz/Atoz/ency/diarrhea.jsp','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:10',NULL,NULL,'15491FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1460,3056,'Clinical or subclinical disturbances of cortical function due to a sudden, abnormal, excessive, and disorganized discharge of brain cells. Clinical manifestations include abnormal motor, sensory and psychic phenomena. Recurrent seizures are usually referred to as EPILEPSY or seizure disorder','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:10',NULL,NULL,'3302FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1461,3057,'A focal dystonia characterized by a sustained spasmodic contraction of neck muscles. The trapezius and sternocleidomastoid muscles are primarily involved, resulting in twisting of the neck and an unnatural position of the head. Torticollis may occur as a primary disease process or in association with another condition (e.g., NECK INJURIES, the use of ANTIPSYCHOTIC AGENTS, etc.). (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, p107)','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:10',NULL,NULL,'3297FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1462,3058,'ToxÃ©mie GravÃ©dique','fr',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:10',NULL,NULL,'3295FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1463,3058,'Pregnancy-induced hypertensive states, including EPH gestosis when edema and proteinuria accompany hypertension. Other hypertensive disorders that develop during pregnancy or the puerperium are pre-eclampsia and eclampsia, either of which may be superimposed upon chronic hypertensive vascular or renal disease.','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:10',NULL,NULL,'3294FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
