(1470,3067,'Compulsion to pull out one&amp;#39;s hair.','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:11',NULL,NULL,'3261FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1471,3069,'A subgroup of PARAPSORIASIS itself divided into acute and chronic forms. The acute form is characterized by the abrupt onset of a generalized, reddish-brown, maculopapular eruption. Lesions may be vesicular, hemorrhagic, crusted, or necrotic. Histologically the disease is characterized by epidermal necrolysis. The chronic form shows milder skin changes with necrosis. An important variant of the chronic form is LYMPHOMATOID PAPULOSIS.','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:11',NULL,NULL,'15451FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1472,3070,'Mycobacterial infection of the bone','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:11',NULL,NULL,'16793FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1473,3071,'Inflammation of the tonsils of varying degrees of severity and involving simple inflammation.  Associated with acute pharyngitis, streptococcus infection, or formation of an abscess (as quinsy).','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:11',NULL,NULL,'111FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1474,3073,'Infection of the lymph nodes by tuberculosis. Tuberculous infection of the cervical lymph nodes is scrofula.','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:11',NULL,NULL,'3100FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1475,3077,'Inflammation of the middle ear.','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:11',NULL,NULL,'15396FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1476,3078,'Ulceration of the skin and underlying structures of the lower extremity. About 90% of the cases are due to venous insufficiency (VARICOSE ULCER), 5% to arterial disease, and the remaining 5% to other causes.','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:11',NULL,NULL,'3016FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1477,3079,'A loss of mucous substance of the mouth showing local excavation of the surface, resulting from the sloughing of inflammatory necrotic tissue. It is the result of a variety of causes, e.g., denture irritation, aphthous stomatitis (STOMATITIS, APHTHOUS), NOMA, necrotizing gingivitis (GINGIVITIS, NECROTIZING, ULCERATIVE), TOOTHBRUSHING, and various irritants. (From Jablonski, Dictionary of Dentistry, 1992, p842)','en',2,'2026-08-17 15:51:11',NULL,NULL,'3012FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
